menu "Dongle bridge options"

config DONGLE_FAKE_LINK
	bool "Report synthetic BLE link status"
	default y
	help
	  Reports both remotes as CONNECTED with plausible RSSI and battery
	  values, so the scoreboard's signal and battery indicators can be
	  exercised before any BLE code exists.

	  This changes nothing on the wire — the LINK lines are exactly the
	  ones real remotes would produce. Turn it off to report the truth
	  (both DISCONNECTED) once BLE is implemented.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
